{"availability":"available","full":"Jany-M/airflow-simulator","name":"airflow-simulator","description":"Interactive natural cross-ventilation simulator: draw a floor plan, set the wind, and find the best windows/doors to open, with live temperatures, wind direction and speed","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":10,"forks":1,"created":"2026-08-11T10:15:46Z","updated":"2026-08-30T17:33:33Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://airflowsimulator.netlify.app/","topics":["airflow","floorplan","simulator","weather"],"demo":"https://airflowsimulator.netlify.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T11:07:10.106Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T11:07:10.106Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T11:07:10.106Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T11:07:10.106Z","stars":10,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Interactive web app to simulate natural cross-ventilation. Draw rooms, place windows and doors, get live wind and weather conditions, watch particles flow, and find the optimal configuration that keeps air moving through the floorplan, lowering rooms temperature and humidity.","How and why I built this: From a Real Problem to a Working Web App","The floor plan is treated as a two-dimensional pressure network on a staggered grid. Wind imposes fixed pressures on exterior openings; air flows from high-pressure (windward) to low-pressure (leeward) regions through open doors and windows. The approach belongs to the same family as multizone / airflow-network models used in building science (e.g. CONTAM, EnergyPlus Airflow Network), but uses custom, simplified coefficients tuned for real-time browser performance rather than calibrated engineering output."],"features":["Floor-plan editor — grid rooms (1 cell = 0.5 m, plan 28×18 m), windows/doors on any wall, scale bar, W×L metre inputs, sample plan, erase/rename. Canvas frames the building with minimal padding. Navigation: click-drag…","Select & edit — short click any door/window to open (green) / close (red); long press (0.2 s) to select (yellow ring), then drag the body to move along the wall or the centre dot to resize. Click a room to select; drag…","Live airflow — pressure-network solver + wind particles; percentile heatmap; hover any cell for a live readout (airflow / temp / RH by view mode); per-opening inflow panel labelled by room and wall — click a row to…","Best configuration — searches open/closed sets so wind reaches as many rooms as possible with even cross-ventilation (not one corridor or window hogging inflow); result persists until you edit the plan (synced with live…","Weather — Open-Meteo via geolocation or manual town search (🔍 lens button beside Use my current weather; help (?) explains wrong-location on desktop tethering). Wind compass dial uses a visible grab-hand cursor on the…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Jany-M/airflow-simulator/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"79980a76d00bab0debd291ef87c346ccffa45467d82a4d2297082c5b8951eb43","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T11:07:10.193Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T11:07:10.193Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Interactive web app to simulate natural cross-ventilation. Draw rooms, place windows and doors, get live wind and weather conditions, watch particles flow, and find the optimal configuration that keeps air moving through the floorplan, lowering rooms temperature and humidity.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Jany-M/airflow-simulator/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"79980a76d00bab0debd291ef87c346ccffa45467d82a4d2297082c5b8951eb43","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Jany-M/airflow-simulator/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T11:07:10.193Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-30T17:33:33Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Jany-M/airflow-simulator/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T11:07:10.194Z","hash":"79980a76d00b